/T (Shallow vs deep copy: a shallow copy \(copy.copy, x[:]\) copies only the outer container and shares the inner objects \(output: inner shared: True\). It is enough when all elements are immutable \(numbers, strings, tuples\) or the list is flat. A deep copy is needed for nested mutable data \(list of lists, dict of lists\) when the copy must be completely independent \(inner shared: False\).)
/E (Shallow vs deep copy: a shallow copy \(copy.copy, x[:]\) copies only the outer container and shares the inner objects \(output: inner shared: True\). It is enough when all elements are immutable \(numbers, strings, tuples\) or the list is flat. A deep copy is needed for nested mutable data \(list of lists, dict of lists\) when the copy must be completely independent \(inner shared: False\).)
