/T (Engineering decision \(100,000 complaints/day\): use collections.Counter \(or the dictionary loop\): O\(n\), independent of the vocabulary size, and Counter.most_common\(k\) gives the top-k directly. Never use list.count\(\) for every distinct word, since its cost grows with n x d and real vocabularies have thousands of distinct words.)
/E (Engineering decision \(100,000 complaints/day\): use collections.Counter \(or the dictionary loop\): O\(n\), independent of the vocabulary size, and Counter.most_common\(k\) gives the top-k directly. Never use list.count\(\) for every distinct word, since its cost grows with n x d and real vocabularies have thousands of distinct words.)
