<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 111 0 R
/T (Common students \(n = m\): 1,000: nested 0.0169 s vs set 0.00015 s; 2,000: 0.0659 s vs 0.00034 s; 4,000: 0.254 s vs 0.00057 s. Doubling n makes the nested loops about 4x slower \(O\(n x m\)\) but the set version only about 2x \(O\(n + m\)\). All methods returned the same students.)
/E (Common students \(n = m\): 1,000: nested 0.0169 s vs set 0.00015 s; 2,000: 0.0659 s vs 0.00034 s; 4,000: 0.254 s vs 0.00057 s. Doubling n makes the nested loops about 4x slower \(O\(n x m\)\) but the set version only about 2x \(O\(n + m\)\). All methods returned the same students.)
