/Title (Design question - late reading: insert\(\) costs O\(n\) because later elements shift. It took 1.8 microseconds on 365 items and 14 ms for 100 front-inserts into 365,000 items. For one year of data this is negligible, so a list is still fine \(use bisect.insort to find the position in O\(log n\)\). If very many out-of-order inserts on huge data are expected, switch to a dictionary keyed by date.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1634 0 R
/Prev 1742 0 R
>>
