/Title (One flat list of \(train, name, station, arrival, departure, days\) tuples, scanned for every query: [r for r in flat if r[2] == station and day in r[5]]. Time per query: O\(total stops\) always \(and the whole list is read even for a rare station\), the same order as the nested scan \(0.551 s for 200 queries at 10,000 trains vs 0.666 s nested; the flat scan has no inner loop\) but far above the index \(0.054 s\), which is O\(trains at the station\). Space: flat list O\(total stops\) with repeated train data in every row; nested dictionaries O\(total stops\) with train data stored once; the index adds O\(total stops\) references.)
