/Title (Why a list: readings are ordered by date, accessed by position \(O\(1\)\), sliced easily and only appended to. Costs: append O\(1\) amortised; insert\(i,x\) O\(n\) \(shifts the tail\); pop\(\) O\(1\) from the end, pop\(i\) O\(n\); sort\(\) O\(n log n\).)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1742 0 R
/Prev 1855 0 R
/Next 1920 0 R
>>
endobj
1920 0 obj
<<
/Title (Additions for n readings, window w = 7: naive: each of the \(n-6\) windows needs 6 additions, total 6\(n-6\) \(plus n-6 divisions\) = O\(7n\). Running sum: 6 for the first window, then 1 addition + 1 subtraction per later window, total 6 + 2\(n-7\) = O\(n\). For n = 365,000 that is 2,189,964 vs 729,992, a 3.0x reduction; measured time was 0.174 s vs 0.052 s \(3.3x\), matching the derived ratio.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1742 0 R
/Prev 1919 0 R
/Next 1856 0 R
>>
endobj
