/Title (How a dictionary finds a key: it computes hash\(key\), maps it to a slot in a hash table, compares the stored key and \(if another key is there\) probes the next slot. The table is resized to keep it less than about 2/3 full, so the expected number of probes is a constant that does not depend on how many keys are stored: O\(1\) average lookup \(O\(n\) worst case\).)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1998 0 R
