/Title (Dictionary vs list.count\(\): a dictionary loop touches each of n words once: O\(n\). Calling list.count\(w\) for each of the d distinct words scans the whole list every time: O\(n x d\). Measured with n = 50,000 words: d = 50 gives 0.009 s vs 0.031 s; d = 500 gives 0.005 s vs 0.437 s; d = 5,000 gives 0.006 s vs 3.40 s. The dictionary time stays flat while list.count grows with d.)
/Dest [18 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1998 0 R
/Prev 2035 0 R
/Next 2046 0 R
>>
